// Himat Textile - Realtime Database rules.
//
// Two kinds of person:
//   * OWNER (the app calls them Admin) - listed under super_admins, keyed by email with '.' -> '_'
//     and '@' -> '_at_', or by uid. Only an owner adds or removes an owner.
//   * MEMBER - present and active in the members index.
//
// members is mirrored from employees by the syncMemberIndex Cloud Function and NO client can write
// it. That indirection is the point. Before it existed the rules could only ask "auth != null", so:
//   * any Google account on earth could sign in and read the whole book - customer phone numbers,
//     GSTIN, PAN, bank account and IFSC, every order and cheque; and
//   * employees was client-writable while both apps trusted role: "Admin" on it, so anyone could
//     grant themselves admin with one REST call.
// Now membership comes from a node only the office can write.
//
// Access: every insider reads and writes the whole working set, on purpose. The agency runs one
// shared book - an admin and every staff member must be able to see and continue anybody else's
// trips and orders. Sub Agents are scoped inside the app, not here.
//
// What is locked down:
//   * Nothing is readable without being an insider, except super_admins (the owner check has to run
//     first) and markets (the public supplier form needs the list).
//   * employees is owner-only to write. The role field decides privilege, so it is not client data.
//   * No node can be wiped in one call: writes are allowed per record, never on a whole node.
//   * Only an owner may REMOVE a record. Everyone else can create and update but never delete.
//     Normal deletion goes through the isDeleted flag plus a deletion_requests entry that an owner
//     confirms.
//   * There is no "claim ownership of an empty database" clause. It used to be re-armable.
//   * bin and members are written by Cloud Functions only.
//   * Public registration forms may only create a new request, never read, overwrite or delete one.
//   * Record ids must be numeric strings, matching the client id generator.
//
// Generated by .kiro/backups/gen-rules.ps1 so the long access expressions cannot drift.
